/*!
@defgroup clock_manager
@ingroup mod_system Clock Manager
@brief System and peripheral clock configuration module for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The Clock Manager module provides a unified API for configuring and querying
the entire clock distribution tree of YTMicro MCUs. It manages the System
Clock Unit (SCU), the Inter-Peripheral Crossbar (IPC) peripheral clock gates,
and the Clock Monitor Unit (CMU) for runtime clock integrity monitoring.

@section clock_features Key Features
- Configurable system clock source: FIRC, FXOSC, SIRC, and PLL (device-dependent).
- Independent dividers for Core, Fast Bus, Slow Bus, and Flash clocks.
- Per-peripheral clock gating, source selection, and divider via the IPC subsystem.
- Fast External Oscillator (FXOSC) with bypass mode, gain selection, and
  automatic gain control (ALC) on supported devices.
- Slow External Oscillator (SXOSC) support on select device families.
- Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) with configurable reference divider and feedback
  divider on supported devices.
- Clock Monitor Unit (CMU) for runtime safety monitoring of clock sources
  with configurable high/low thresholds and reset-on-error capability.
- Clock output (CLKOUT) routing for external observation / debugging.
- Clock Manager notification framework: register callbacks to be notified
  before/after clock configuration changes (graceful or forceful policy).
- Runtime clock frequency query for any named clock via CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq().

@section clock_arch Module Architecture

The Clock Manager is organized in a multi-layer architecture that varies
by device family. The YTM32B1Mx variant (representative) is shown below:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Application Code                          │
│          (calls CLOCK_DRV_* / CLOCK_SYS_* functions)        │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          Clock Driver Layer (clock.h / clock_manager.h)      │
│  ● Common API: CLOCK_DRV_Init(), CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq()        │
│  ● Clock Manager: CLOCK_SYS_Init(),                         │
│    CLOCK_SYS_UpdateConfiguration() with callback support     │
├───────────────────┬──────────────────┬───────────────────────┤
│  SCU HW Access    │  IPC HW Access   │  CMU / CFMU HW Access│
│  (scu_hw_access.h)│ (ipc_hw_access.h)│ (cmu_hw_access.h /   │
│  Oscillators, PLL,│ Peripheral clock │  cfmu_hw_access.h)   │
│  Dividers, ClkOut │ gate & source    │ Clock monitoring     │
├───────────────────┴──────────────────┴───────────────────────┤
│                  Clock Hardware (SCU, IPC, CMU)               │
│          (FXOSC, SXOSC, FIRC, SIRC, PLL, Dividers)          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection clock_arch_driver Driver Layer (clock.h / clock_manager.h)
Application code should use the `CLOCK_DRV_*` functions for basic initialization
and frequency queries. For multi-configuration systems with callback support,
use the `CLOCK_SYS_*` API (init configuration table, update configuration by
index with graceful/forceful policy).

@subsection clock_arch_hw HW Access Layer
This internal layer provides low-level inline register accessors organized
by hardware sub-block:
- **SCU** — System clock source selection, divider configuration, oscillator
  control (FXOSC/SXOSC), PLL configuration, and clock output routing.
- **IPC** — Peripheral clock gate enable/disable, clock source selection,
  and divider configuration per peripheral.
- **CMU / CFMU** — Clock Monitor Unit channel enable, reference clock
  selection, threshold configuration, and frequency measurement (CFMU).

@section clock_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection clock_config_scu scu_config_t Fields (System Clock Configuration)
| Field              | Type                    | Description                                                           |
|--------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| sircDeepSleepEnable| bool                    | Keep SIRC running in deep-sleep mode.                                 |
| sircStandbyEnable  | bool                    | Keep SIRC running in standby mode.                                    |
| sircPowerDownEnable| bool                    | Keep SIRC running in power-down mode (device-dependent).              |
| fircEnable         | bool                    | Enable the Fast Internal RC oscillator (48 MHz).                      |
| fircDeepSleepEnable| bool                    | Keep FIRC running in deep-sleep mode.                                 |
| sysClkSrc          | scu_system_clock_src_t  | System clock source: FIRC / PLL / FXOSC / SIRC.                      |
| fxoscConfig        | scu_fxosc_config_t      | Fast external oscillator configuration.                               |
| sxoscConfig        | scu_sxosc_config_t      | Slow external oscillator configuration (if FEATURE_SCU_SUPPORT_SXOSC).|
| pllConfig          | scu_pll_config_t        | PLL configuration (if FEATURE_SCU_SUPPORT_PLL).                       |
| sysDiv             | uint8_t                 | System (core) clock divider (0 = /1, 1 = /2, ... 15 = /16).          |
| fastBusDiv         | uint8_t                 | Fast bus clock divider.                                               |
| slowBusDiv         | uint8_t                 | Slow bus clock divider.                                               |
| flashDiv           | uint8_t                 | Flash clock divider (EFM RWS).                                       |
| flashPrs           | uint8_t                 | Flash clock prescaler.                                                |
| clockOutConfig     | scu_clock_out_config_t  | Clock output pin configuration (source, divider, enable).             |

@subsection clock_config_pll scu_pll_config_t Fields
| Field          | Type               | Description                                                |
|----------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| enable         | bool               | Enable PLL.                                                |
| pllRefClock    | scu_pll_ref_clk_t  | PLL reference: SCU_PLL_REF_FXOSC_CLK or SCU_PLL_REF_FIRC_CLK. |
| pllFeedBackDiv | uint8_t            | PLL feedback divider (Ndiv). Fout = Fref * Ndiv / (2 * Npre). |
| pllRefClkDiv   | uint8_t            | PLL reference clock divider (Npre).                        |

@subsection clock_config_ipc peripheral_clock_config_t Fields
| Field    | Type                        | Description                                          |
|----------|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| clkName  | clock_names_t               | Peripheral clock name (e.g., IPC_SPI0_CLOCK).        |
| clkGate  | bool                        | Enable (true) or disable (false) the peripheral clock.|
| clkSrc   | peripheral_clock_source_t   | Clock source: FIRC / SIRC / FXOSC / PLL / etc.       |
| divider  | peripheral_clock_divider_t  | Divider value (DIV_BY_1 ... DIV_BY_16).              |

@subsection clock_config_cmu cmu_ch_config_t Fields
| Field       | Type         | Description                                                      |
|-------------|--------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| enable      | bool         | Enable this CMU monitoring channel.                              |
| resetEnable | bool         | Generate system reset on clock error detection.                  |
| refClock    | cmu_refclk_t | Reference clock: CMU_REF_SIRC_CLOCK or CMU_REF_FXOSC_CLOCK.     |
| compareHigh | uint16_t     | Upper frequency threshold (counter compare value).               |
| compareLow  | uint16_t     | Lower frequency threshold (counter compare value).               |

@subsection clock_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                          | Description                                               |
|--------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_SCU_FIRC_FREQ          | FIRC frequency in Hz (typically 48 MHz).                  |
| FEATURE_SCU_SIRC_FREQ          | SIRC frequency in Hz (typically 8 MHz).                   |
| FEATURE_SCU_SUPPORT_PLL        | Set to 1 if device supports PLL.                          |
| FEATURE_SCU_SUPPORT_SXOSC      | Set to 1 if device supports slow external oscillator.     |
| FEATURE_SCU_SUPPORT_LPO        | Set to 1 if device supports low-power oscillator.         |
| FEATURE_CLOCK_TIMEOUT_LOOP_CNT | Timeout loop count for clock switch / PLL lock wait.      |

@section clock_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection clock_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic Clock Initialization
The most common usage: configure system clock source, dividers, and peripheral
clocks, then call CLOCK_DRV_Init().

@code{.c}
/* Clock configuration (typically generated by config tool) */
const scu_config_t scuConfig = {
    .sircDeepSleepEnable = true,
    .sircStandbyEnable   = false,
    .fircEnable          = true,
    .fircDeepSleepEnable = false,
    .sysClkSrc           = SCU_SYSTEM_CLOCK_SRC_FIRC,
    .fxoscConfig = {
        .enable    = true,
        .bypassMode = false,
        .frequency = 8000000U,  /* 8 MHz crystal */
    },
    .sysDiv     = 0U,   /* Core = SysClkSrc / 1 */
    .fastBusDiv = 0U,   /* Fast bus = Core / 1 */
    .slowBusDiv = 1U,   /* Slow bus = Fast bus / 2 */
    .flashDiv   = 1U,
    .clockOutConfig = { .enable = false },
};

const peripheral_clock_config_t periClocks[] = {
    { .clkName = IPC_SPI0_CLOCK, .clkGate = true,
      .clkSrc = CLK_SRC_FIRC,   .divider = DIV_BY_1 },
    { .clkName = IPC_UART0_CLOCK, .clkGate = true,
      .clkSrc = CLK_SRC_FIRC,    .divider = DIV_BY_2 },
};

const ipc_config_t ipcConfig = {
    .count = 2U,
    .peripheralClocks = periClocks,
};

const clock_user_config_t clockConfig = {
    .scuConfigPtr = &scuConfig,
    .cmuConfigPtr = NULL,   /* Use default CMU settings */
    .ipcConfig    = ipcConfig,
};

/* Initialize clocks */
status_t status = CLOCK_DRV_Init(&clockConfig);
@endcode

@subsection clock_usage_manager Pattern 2: Multi-Configuration with Clock Manager
Use the Clock Manager framework for systems that switch between multiple clock
configurations at runtime, with callback notifications.

@code{.c}
/* Pre-defined clock configurations (e.g., RUN and LOW_POWER) */
const clock_user_config_t *g_clockConfigs[] = {
    &clockConfig_RUN,
    &clockConfig_LOW_POWER,
};
#define CLOCK_CONFIG_COUNT  2U

/* Callback configuration */
clock_manager_callback_user_config_t *g_clockCallbacks[] = { NULL };

/* Step 1: Install configuration table */
CLOCK_SYS_Init(g_clockConfigs, CLOCK_CONFIG_COUNT,
               g_clockCallbacks, 0U);

/* Step 2: Apply first configuration (RUN mode) */
CLOCK_SYS_UpdateConfiguration(0U, CLOCK_MANAGER_POLICY_FORCIBLE);

/* Step 3: Later, switch to LOW_POWER configuration */
CLOCK_SYS_UpdateConfiguration(1U, CLOCK_MANAGER_POLICY_AGREEMENT);
@endcode

@subsection clock_usage_freq Pattern 3: Query Clock Frequency
Retrieve the current frequency of any named clock at runtime.

@code{.c}
uint32_t coreFreq, spiFreq;

/* Get core clock frequency */
CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq(CORE_CLK, &coreFreq);

/* Get SPI0 peripheral clock frequency */
CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq(IPC_SPI0_CLOCK, &spiFreq);
@endcode

@subsection clock_usage_peri Pattern 4: Dynamic Peripheral Clock Control
Change a single peripheral's clock source and divider at runtime without
re-initializing the entire clock tree.

@code{.c}
/* Reconfigure UART0 clock: switch to FXOSC, divider /4 */
CLOCK_DRV_SetModuleClock(IPC_UART0_CLOCK, true,
                         (uint32_t)CLK_SRC_FXOSC,
                         (uint32_t)DIV_BY_4);

/* Reset UART0 module after clock change */
CLOCK_DRV_ResetModule(IPC_UART0_CLOCK);
@endcode

@section clock_api API Quick Reference

@subsection clock_api_init Initialization
| Function                         | Description                                                         |
|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| CLOCK_DRV_Init()                 | Initialize system and peripheral clocks from configuration struct.  |
| CLOCK_SYS_Init()                 | Install clock configuration table and callbacks for Clock Manager.  |

@subsection clock_api_config Configuration & Switching
| Function                         | Description                                                         |
|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| CLOCK_SYS_UpdateConfiguration()  | Switch to a pre-defined clock configuration by index with policy.   |
| CLOCK_SYS_SetConfiguration()     | Apply a clock configuration struct directly (wrapper of CLOCK_DRV_Init). |
| CLOCK_DRV_SetModuleClock()       | Set individual peripheral clock gate, source, and divider.          |
| CLOCK_DRV_ResetModule()          | Assert and de-assert software reset for a peripheral via IPC.       |

@subsection clock_api_query Frequency Query & Status
| Function                            | Description                                               |
|-------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq()                 | Get clock frequency in Hz for any named clock.            |
| CLOCK_SYS_GetFreq()                 | Wrapper of CLOCK_DRV_GetFreq() (legacy API).              |
| CLOCK_SYS_GetCurrentConfiguration() | Get index of the currently active clock configuration.    |
| CLOCK_SYS_GetErrorCallback()        | Get the callback that returned error during last switch.  |
| CLOCK_SYS_WaitFXOSCValid()          | Wait for FXOSC startup to complete (with gain sweep).     |

@subsection clock_api_measure Clock Measurement (Device-Dependent)
| Function                         | Description                                                         |
|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| CLOCK_SYS_MeasureClkFreq()       | Measure frequency of a specified clock source via CFMU hardware.    |

@section clock_notes Important Notes

@subsection clock_notes_order Initialization Order
@warning The clock module must be initialized **before** any peripheral driver
that depends on a peripheral clock. Call CLOCK_DRV_Init() at the very
beginning of the application startup, before initializing SPI, UART, CRC, etc.

@subsection clock_notes_fxosc FXOSC Startup
@note When FXOSC is enabled, the driver performs an automatic gain sweep and
waits for the oscillator valid flag. If the FXOSC crystal does not start
within FEATURE_CLOCK_TIMEOUT_LOOP_CNT iterations, STATUS_SCU_FXOSC_READY_TIMEOUT
is returned.

@subsection clock_notes_pll PLL Lock
@warning When PLL is enabled, the driver waits for PLL lock with a periodic
toggle recovery mechanism. If lock is not achieved within the timeout,
STATUS_SCU_PLL_LOCK_TIMEOUT is returned and the system clock remains on SIRC.

@subsection clock_notes_switch Clock Switching Sequence
The driver internally follows this sequence during CLOCK_DRV_Init():
1. Configure peripheral clocks (IPC) — set gates and sources.
2. Switch system clock to SIRC as a safe intermediate source.
3. Configure oscillators (FXOSC, SXOSC) and PLL.
4. Set system dividers and wait for divider stability.
5. Switch to the target system clock source.
6. Configure CMU monitoring channels.
7. Update SystemCoreClock and flash prescaler.

@note Do **not** disable the clock source that is currently selected as the
system clock. The driver handles the SIRC fallback automatically.

@subsection clock_notes_cmu CMU Default Configuration
When `cmuConfigPtr` is NULL, the driver enables CMU with a ±25% tolerance
around the expected clock frequency, using SIRC as the reference clock.
To disable CMU entirely, define `CMU_DEFAULT_OFF` before including the
clock headers.

@subsection clock_notes_callbacks Callback Notifications
When using CLOCK_SYS_UpdateConfiguration() with CLOCK_MANAGER_POLICY_AGREEMENT,
all registered BEFORE callbacks must return STATUS_SUCCESS for the switch to
proceed. If any callback returns an error, the switch is aborted and
STATUS_MCU_NOTIFY_BEFORE_ERROR is returned. Use CLOCK_SYS_GetErrorCallback()
to identify which callback failed.

@section clock_integration Integration Guide

@subsection clock_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source file must be added to the project build (example for YTM32B1Mx):
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/clock/YTM32B1Mx/clock_YTM32B1Mx.c
@endverbatim

@subsection clock_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directories to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/clock/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/clock/YTM32B1Mx/   (device-specific)
@endverbatim

@subsection clock_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
| Symbol              | Description                                             |
|---------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| CMU_DEFAULT_OFF     | Define to disable automatic CMU configuration.          |
| CPU / SERIES macros | Device-specific macro (e.g., YTM32B1M_SERIES) to select clock implementation. |

@subsection clock_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref interrupt_manager — Required for disabling/enabling global interrupts during clock transitions.

*/
